B.XQ=new A.b9(B.Yp,["Defeat enemies","Defeat bosses","Catch Golden Heralds","Open chests","Tap attacks","Use Whirlwind","Upgrade stats","The Forgotten Graveyard","Where it slept for so long. The march on the castle begins.","The Dark Forest","A hundred years ago, the Hero's army hid here and waited.","The Burned Village","The kingdom's edge. The castle towers draw near.","Before the Castle","The old Demon King's Castle. The King lives there now.","Leon","\u26a0 Block it!","\ud83d\udc51 The King","\ud83d\udcab Stunned","\ud83d\udcab Opening!","\ud83d\udc7f The Command","Boss","+{v} gold","Soul stones +{soulStones}","Swordsman","Guardian","Berserker","{v} Tier {tier}!","\u26a0 Overhead Strike! Tap the boss to block","Upgraded!","{flurryName} (auto)","Fifth!","Ben blocked it!","Ben took it on his back","Ella held you up!","Held on!","\u2728 Golden Herald! Tap to catch","The next Royal Guard Captain blocks the gate!","Blocked!","Overhead Strike!","Counter! {v}","Best stage {bestStage}","Can't choose yet","Can change the next time you sleep","Can't change while fighting a boss","Can change in {v}s","Dad","Rattle","Skeleton","Now \xb7 Epilogue \u201c{title}\u201d","Now \xb7 {v} \u201c{title}\u201d","Prologue","Ch. {ch}","The Teacher's Memory","The Father's Memory","Memory in the Flames","Memory of a Small Hand","The Broken Command","Memory of the Command",'"Same spot. Five times."',"\u2026The bones know this swordplay.","\u2026Welcome home.","In a burning house, it lifted a baby.","A small hand held on to a finger bone.","Arms that once carried something.","\u2026No.","Don't think. Just cut. \u2014 the Demon King's last command","Rage.","Blocked {smashBreaks} strikes by hand","Spent a long time away","Hardly ever blocked a strike by hand","\u2014 the Demon King's last command","Where the child sleeps. The flowers never run out.","There are graveyards all over the kingdom. Those who haven't made it home yet.","The King did not die. Soldiers carried him to the next castle.","Drops of violet light lie along the road.","A graveyard everyone forgot. All but one.","No one at the cabin. Who will mend the roof now?","Fresh straw on the cabin roof. Someone mended it yesterday.","More than a hundred years ago, the child walked out of this forest and became the Hero.","The forest where the Hero's army hid. It smells familiar.","Wildflower Village. Houses are going up, one by one.","Ben stopped at a door, then walked on.","The place I burned.","An empty castle. No banner flies.","The highest window is dark.","The highest window is lit again tonight.","The old Demon King's Castle. The child lives here.","For {away}, {who}","While you were away","\ud83d\udd4a Sent home {sentHome} / {owed}","\ud83d\udc80 {toCastle} stages to the next castle","\ud83d\udc51 To the child.","\ud83d\udc51 {toCastle} stages to the child","\ud83d\udd6f Embers {soulPower} \xb7 {toCastle} stages to the child","{className} Tier {tier}!","\u201c{v}\u201d found its name","\ud83d\udd13 Unlocked: {v}!","Boss!","This try: {v}% of the boss's HP (best {v2}%)","Fell\u2026 trying Stage {stage} again","When the boss rears back, tap it yourself to block the strike","Stuck? Raise HP and Attack in the Grow tab","Got soul stones? Upgrade your bones in the Bones tab","Sleep to grow stronger for good with embers (Sleep tab)","The skeleton fights while you are away. Take a break; the gold piles up","{inHours}h {v}m","{inMinutes}m","\n{v}\n(up to {inHours} hours)","Collect","\ud83c\udf19 Awake \xb7 embers +{gained}","From the grave, it walks again, stronger.","\ud83d\udc51 The gate is open","Keep fighting","About sleeping"," (+{inheritedLevel} carried over)","\ud83d\udc80 Equipped {name}!{carried}","{name} fused +1","No enemies nearby.","Coming soon","Not open yet.","This feature is on its way.","Close the game?","The skeleton keeps fighting while it is closed.","Keep playing","Close","\ud83d\udcd6 The Book of Memories opened","Read remembered scenes again from \ud83d\udcd6 at the top right","Area and goal","\ud83e\udde0 Choose a Calling","Grow","Bones","Calling","Quests","Sleep","Knock","Settings","Book of Memories","Ben \xb7 Ella","Ben","Auto Tap","\ud83d\udc46 Tap to attack!","\u2014 below, in another hand","Days walked together","{days}","Those you struck down","{v}","Visits to the child","{kingVisits}","Strikes blocked","{smashBreaks}","Letters received","{length}/9","Times slept","{rebirths}","Hours you watched","{v} h","Hours Rattle waited","Sent home","{sentHome}","Rattle's Record","(This record stays on this device only)","Walk on","Gravekeeper","Forest Warden","Garrison Captain","The Royal Guard's gate","The Border Guard's Gate","Border {rank}","Toby's daughter, herald","Toby the herald ({v})","\u2709 Letter \u2014 {from}","\u2014 Leon","\ud83d\udcdc Royal Decree","Soldiers sometimes, and bosses always, drop the bone they carried.\nBetter bones equip themselves \xb7 same grade stacks +1 \xb7 weaker ones break into soul stones\nSoul stones: the warmth left in broken bones. Used to strengthen bones.\nTap a fitted bone to see what it remembers.","\u2026Nothing comes back yet.","{label} (empty)","Raises {statLabel} \xb7 dropped by enemies","Upgrade {label} bone, {enhanceCost} soul stones","Upgrades","No progress","Your Google account has further progress","Google account","This phone","The progress you don't choose will be lost.","Keep this phone's","Load the account's","In its sleep, it dreamed.","Only one comes along on this walk.","Stage {stage} boss","{v} \xb7 best {bestStage}","{v} \xb7 best Stage {bestStage}","Close","{title} +{others} more","\ud83d\udc51 The battle with the King!","\ud83d\udc51 {toCastle} stages to the castle","\ud83c\udf19 Sleep now for embers +{rebirthReward}","\ud83d\udd6f Embers {soulPower} \xb7 {toCastle} stages to the next castle","Gold","Soul stones","Sent home: {sentHome}","The child is waiting.","Next memory: walk to Stage {gate}, then sleep again","Next memory: when morning comes, sleep again (after 6 a.m.)","The next memory comes after you sleep again.","\ud83d\udcd6 Book of Memories","Dev build: preview every memory (the save is not changed)","Memories","Letters","Royal Decrees","Bone Memories","The Red Voice","Clack Dictionary","Opening","Last Words","Epilogue \xb7 {v}","The Demon King's Ending","A memory not yet returned","New memory","(They were the child's parents.)","(The King knew the two skeletons.)","Ben and Ella never threw a bone at the King. {answer}","\u2709 Letter {v}","\ud83d\udcdc Royal Decree {v}","{v} {label} Bone","Sounds with no meaning yet.","Ella","\ud83d\udc46 Hands-on","\ud83d\udca4 Idle","\u26a0 Risky","Suggested","{v}Tier {tier} \u201c{title}\u201d","Remembered Calling","No memory held yet","{v} \xb7 Tier {tier} \u201c{v2}\u201d","\u2726 Becomes Tier {pending} when you next wake","Every tier has returned","When you next wake: ","Choose a memory","With this memory: {runs} runs \xb7 best Stage {best} \xb7 King defeated {kings}","Memory held now","Cancel","Held from your next waking","Hold this memory","Change it any time before your first sleep","Fight with this memory","Later","Back","Start","Skip","Tap to go back","Tap to start","Tap to skip","Today's quests \xb7 new at midnight","{label} \xd7{target}","All-clear bonus","Done","Embers","Attack \xb7 HP \xb7 Gold +{v}%","Slept {rebirths} times","Best this run: Stage {runBest} \u2192 embers +{reward}","\ud83c\udf19 Sleep again (+{reward})","\ud83c\udf19 Sleep again","Left behind","Stage, Attack/HP/Crit levels, gold","Kept","Embers, bones, soul stones, calling, unlocked features, quests","Sleep again?","Return to the grave, sleep, and wake at Stage 1.\nBorrowed strength (upgrade levels, gold) stays behind;\nthe embers you gathered (+{reward}) stay forever.","Cancel","Tier {pending} \u2726new","Tier {tier}","Memory on waking \xb7 ","Sound","Sound on","Music","Effects","Play","Vibration","Auto-advance memory scenes","When off, tap to go on. After 20 seconds without input they advance on their own.","How to play","Watch the opening again","Comfort","Larger text","No screen shake","Save","Changing devices or deleting the app loses your progress. Copy the backup code and keep it somewhere safe (a note, or a message to yourself).","Copy backup code","Load from backup code","Start over","\ud83e\uddea Test saves (dev builds only)","Erases the current progress and jumps to the start of the chosen chapter. For checking screens.","Ch. 1 \xb7 before sleep","Ch. 7 \xb7 last morning (Stage 48)","Ch. 7 \xb7 last morning","Forest","Forest boss","Village","Village boss","Castle","Royal Guard"," gen.","About","{title} {version}\nMade by {developer} \xb7 {contactEmail}","Privacy policy","Open-source licenses","Effective {privacyEffective}","Go further and new things open up; they will be written here too.","Sign in to Google Play Games to save your progress to your account, so you can carry on after changing phones or reinstalling.","Sign in to Google Play Games","Backup code copied ({length} characters)","Your current progress will be replaced by the backup code's.","Paste DGR1:\u2026","Not a valid backup code","Load","The current progress will be erased.","Go","All progress will be erased: stages, gold, bones, embers, callings and story.\nThis cannot be undone. Copy your backup code first.","Erase all","{label}, ready in {secondsLeft}s","A cart stands by the road ahead.\nMeet Old Whetstone to upgrade.","Attack (Lv.{v})","Hones the weapon","Max HP (Lv.{v})","Binds the joints","Crit Chance (Lv.{v})","Sharpens the point","Crit Damage (Lv.{v})","Weights the edge","Attack Speed (Lv.{v})","Shaves it lighter","Upgrade {title}, costs {costLabel} gold","Old Whetstone","You haven't seen this scene yet. Skip it?","Keep watching","Skip \u25b8\u25b8","Tap to close","Tap to continue \u25b8","A new version is out","You can keep playing while it downloads.","Update","Downloading the new version","We'll let you know here when it's ready.","The new version is ready","Restart to update. Your progress is saved.","Restart","+{gold} gold{capped}","The King fell.\n{extra}\nSoldiers carried him out of the castle on their backs.\nThe gate was left open.\n\nBut this skeleton has not yet won back its old strength.\nSleep in the grave, and the embers it gathered will settle; it will wake stronger.","Best stage {bestStage} \xb7 {kills} defeated"," \xb7 slept {rebirths}\xd7","Reach Stage {stage} to sleep.\nThe farther you go, the more embers you gather.","Rattle: Skeleton Idle RPG","Yulmu","November 19, 2026","Personal information we collect",'The developer of Rattle: Skeleton Idle RPG (the "game") does not collect or keep any personal information: no names, contact details, location or device identifiers.',"What is stored on your device","Your progress (stages, upgrades, bones, story and so on) and settings are stored on this device. Unless you use the Google Play Games save below, they are deleted when you uninstall the app.","Google Play Games save (Android)",'When you are signed in to Google Play Games, the Android app also saves your progress and settings to "Saved Games" in that Google account, so you can carry on after changing phones or reinstalling. This data is kept on Google\'s servers and the developer cannot see it. It is handled under the Google Privacy Policy (policies.google.com/privacy). If you are not signed in, nothing is sent. You can delete the saved data in the Google Play Games app or your Google account settings.',"Deleting your data","Your progress lives in two places. The progress on this device is deleted when you uninstall the app. The progress saved to your Google Play Games account is deleted when you delete this game's data in the Google Play Games app's profile settings or at play.google.com/games/profile. The developer keeps none of this data, so there is nothing to request from the developer. Send any questions to the contact address below.","Internet use","Apart from the Google Play Games save above, the game does not use the internet. It has no ads, analytics or payments.","Backup code",'"Copy backup code" in the settings only turns your progress into text and copies it to the clipboard; where you keep that code is up to you. The game does not store or send the code.',"Sharing with third parties","The developer collects nothing, so nothing is shared with third parties. The Google Play Games save is between your signed-in Google account and Google.","Children","The game does not collect personal information from children either.","Changes to this policy","If a feature that handles information (such as ads) is ever added, this policy will be updated before it takes effect, with notice in the game and on this page.","Contact","Yulmu \xb7 chw3448@gmail.com","Hero's","Soldier's","Knight's","Captain's","Head","Crit Damage","Chest","Max HP","Arm","Attack","Leg","Attack Speed","Pocket Money","Gold +50%","Dream of the Great Sword","Damage to bosses +30%","Scent of Wildflowers","Mending (healing) \xd72","Light Hands","Block Overhead Strikes in 4 taps","Tag","Golden Heralds come twice as often","Sound of the Whetstone","Crit Chance +5 pts","Fighting","The skeleton fights on its own. Tap to strike the front enemy together.\nSoldiers come in threes, two at a time. Beat nine and the boss appears.","Mending","Between fights the skeleton puts its scattered bones back together and slowly regains HP. It does not heal while fighting.\nIf it falls, it pulls itself together and fights the stage again from the start.","The boss's Overhead Strike","When the boss rears back, an Overhead Strike is coming. Tap the boss 5 times before it lands to block it, and the boss staggers for a moment.\nIf you miss, it hits several times harder than usual.","Five steps from the castle (Stage 45), three Royal Guard Captains block the gate one after another. Get past them for triple soul stones.","Pay Old Whetstone by the road in gold and he hones your weapon (Attack), binds your joints (HP) and sharpens the point (Crit). Stuck? Check the Grow tab first.","Old Whetstone's Craft","A heavier edge raises Crit Damage; a lighter one raises Attack Speed. Both reset when you sleep.","Skills","Use them with the buttons at the bottom. After using one, wait for it to fill up again.","Equip Bones","Bosses always drop a bone; soldiers sometimes do. Fit one each to skull, ribcage, arm and leg.\nAnother of the same grade makes the fitted bone stronger (+1); lower grades break down into soul stones.","Golden Herald","Now and then a golden herald runs past. The skeleton won't chase it, so tap it yourself. Every hit drops gold, and catching it pays big.","Ben and Ella","Two skeletons risen from their graves throw bones at your side. They only hit enemies fighting you, and never the King.","The skeleton strikes without you touching the screen. Only your own taps can block a boss's Overhead Strike, though.","Treasure Chest","Soldiers sometimes drop a chest. Tap it open for gold or soul stones.","Daily Quests","Three new goals every day. Clear them for soul stones.","Choose one way of fighting the bones remember. Each memory fights differently.\nMemories deepen as the story goes on (tiers 2 and 3) and stay when you sleep. You can pick another path the next time you sleep.","The skeleton keeps fighting while the app is closed. Come back to collect gold (up to 8 hours).","Go back to the grave and sleep, and you wake again at Stage 1. Borrowed strength (upgrade levels, gold) stays behind; the embers you picked up on the road stay forever and raise everything.\nThe farther you go, the more you gather. When you feel stuck, it is time to sleep.\nThe next memory only returns once you walk to a set stage (shown in the Sleep tab). Sleep before that and only a few days pass.","Flash Cut","Breakthrough","Onslaught","Whirlwind","Frenzy","Flurry","Blocks the Overhead Strike and strikes back","Counter","Block a strike with your own taps to counter (always a crit)","Boss stun after a block 2s \u2192 3s","Five Times","Hit the boss 5 times, each within 0.4s,","and the 5th tap always crits, damage \xd73","The Wooden Sword","Bosses stunned by your block take \xd71.5 damage","(except Flash Cut)","Takes hits, won't fall","Take It on the Back","Half damage from unblocked strikes","Max HP +20%","Taking a strike lights \ud83d\udee1 \u2192 survive 1 killing blow","(goes out when you block a strike yourself)","A Hand to Hold You Up","With Ella: \ud83d\udee1 holds twice","The second one heals 25% HP","He Who Guarded the Door","Ben blocks 1 in 2 boss strikes","He won't block the King's strikes yet","Ben takes half of 1 in 3 of the King's strikes","Stronger when hurt","Max HP \u221210%","\u26a0 Damage taken in Frenzy \xd71.2","The command is broken \u2014 no price","Rage","Attack +0.5% per 1% HP lost (max +40%)","Don't Think","Frenzy 10s \u2192 15s","In boss fights, below 50% HP, 3s without tapping triggers Frenzy","Cut","Frenzy cooldown 60s \u2192 40s","In boss fights, Frenzy Attack bonus at least +40%","Unlocks after: {condition}","Unlocks at Stage {stage}","A wide bone swing that hits every enemy hard","Mend your body with the bones soldiers carry","Tap the golden herald who runs past now and then (gold with every hit)","The skeleton who guarded the door fights at your side","Attack Speed \xd72 for 10 seconds","3 automatic tap attacks per second","The skeleton who shielded the child stands with you too","Tap open the chests enemies sometimes drop","Clear 3 daily goals for soul stones",'"I\'ll do this for you too, now." Heavier edge (Crit Damage) or lighter (Attack Speed)',"Choose a way of fighting the bones remember","Beat the Stage 40 boss","Sleep in your grave and grow stronger for good with the embers you gathered","Defeat the King","The March","I'm Home","The Name","The Rib","Three","Sorry I Woke You","The Next Morning","Seeing Them Home","When the Demon King's\nCastle fell,","his strongest skeleton\nwas shattered\nby the Hero's sword.","\u2026A hundred years later,","in a forgotten graveyard,\none piece of bone\nbegins to move again,","gripping a bone\nthat lay by the grave.","a child, weeping,\ncut down the skeleton\nwho raised him.",'The skeleton gave its last spark\nto the child.\n"Live."',"\u2026And for more than a hundred years,\nthe child could not die.","one finger bone\nthat a baby once held.","Bring down the king. Take back the castle.","The child waited a hundred years.","The First Story","The Truth of That Day","Knock.","His Majesty's waiting./Everyone stood aside this time.","Those who swore an oath/blocked the road again today.","Take it back.","Don't think. Just cut.","Cut.","Bring him down.","White wildflowers on the grave./Not wilted.","Bones remember. Even broken.","This forest\u2026 a smell it knows./Without a nose.","\u2026The last piece of bone/did not break this time either.","Violet light lies on the road./Each piece warmed the bones.","\u2026Dad. A word never heard/from that child.","Another command/broke.","Clack.","\u2026It's you.","Clack, clack-clack.","Let's go. To him.","The flowers are still here.","Clack\u2026 clack.","That's him.","\u2026He grew up.","Clack-clack!","Get up.","Tally marks covered the pillar.","A few tally marks, cut deep.","At the grave,\n{n} letters never received.","\u2026A year later.\nI rose at the child's feet\nand laid flowers on the grave.","Toby's daughter padded\nher dad's armor. Still too big.","A third house\nin Wildflower Village.\nI didn't build it.","Toby burned the goat milk.\nI laughed.\nIt sounded like a rattle.","Someone mended the cabin roof.\nThere's no decree anymore.","Toby's daughter\nbecame a squire.","The wildflowers bloomed.","We dug a well in the village.","The graveyard never lacks flowers.","Toby grew old.\nThe goat has not changed.","Toby's daughter had a child.\nThe skeleton drawing\nwas passed down.","\u2026\u2026. \u2026You came.","\u2026Yes./Like that.","\u2026Not yet, huh.","Ten years. \u2026You came/sooner than I thought.","That's it./Don't be scared.","It's fine./Block it next time.","That sound\u2026/You remember?","Yes./Same spot.","Five times./Don't forget.","When the big sword rises,/don't flinch. Your words.","\u2026Well done.","Going easy/teaches nothing, you said.","Remember this sword?","\u2026Rattle./Same sound as ever.","It's your rib./Still sharp.","You two\u2026/At last I can greet you.","\u2026I'm nervous./Everyone's watching.","It's fine./There's still time.","\u2026I'm sorry./For waking you.","You've gotten good./Really.","Not many more/of these left.","It's still night./\u2026Go back to sleep.","Back again./\u2026Take your time this time.","Back again.","I'm a little out of breath.","You came all this way./Thank you.","\u2026At the next castle.","All the way here again./They carried me on their backs.","A king who gets carried around./Funny, right?","Everyone went first./My friends. My wife.","This is how it was for you./Seeing them off. Left alone.","If that day I hadn't/struck the fifth time\u2014","No. You wouldn't/have wanted that.","Rat\u2026 \u2026Your name/keeps slipping away.","It's fine./As long as you remember.","You're here?/\u2026Flowers.","\u26a0 Same spot. Five times!","This time, with your own hand.","It's okay.","I'm used/to waiting.","Take your time.","\u2026It's okay.","Yes. It's all right.","Five times, right.","Cut. Cut.","Those flowers on the grave\u2014/I didn't put them there.","Must tell\u2026/His Majesty\u2026","My father/died here.","The flowers\u2026/His Majesty\u2026","My grandfather. My father./They stopped you here.","My family\u2026/guards the graves\u2026","Royal decree. No one/touches that cabin.","The roof\u2026/needs mending\u2026","I mended the roof again./By royal decree.","Why does His Majesty\u2026/that cabin\u2026","Three generations now/mending that roof.","Notches on the doorframe\u2026/His Majesty's height\u2026","I mended the roof yesterday./He said it was the last time.","\u2026Go./His Majesty is waiting.","A hundred years ago/the Hero shattered you.","That block\u2026/His Majesty taught me\u2026","His Majesty\u2026/was waiting\u2026","An oath sworn to the King/not even he can take back.","\u2026So you block it.","I kept\u2026/my oath\u2026","This village has stood like this/a hundred years. By decree.","He said not to/rebuild\u2026 The reason\u2026","Have you seen it all?/His Majesty wanted you to.","\u2026Same spot./Five times.","This village was called/Wildflower.","I received a decree./His last request, he said.","His Majesty's\u2026/last decree\u2026","His Majesty is waiting./Still, I hold this far.","\u2026Pass.","One\u2026","Two\u2026","Three!","O-one\u2026","T-two\u2026","Threeee!","Eek!/His Majesty said only count to three!","Gold!/I'll give you gold!","And a letter\u2026/there's a letter too!","I'm a recruit now!/So I'm even more scared!","We meet again!/\u2026Uh, I'll run now!","I got married!/\u2026Oh, here's a letter.","My wife says/hello, sir.","My daughter left a skeleton/drawing at your grave.","His Majesty smiles these days./Whenever you come up.","I'm Knight-Captain now./But I still deliver!","I shouldn't run\u2026/My legs go first!",'His Majesty keeps/saying "Rattle" lately.',"His Majesty's legs are bad./My daughter goes next year.","It's Dad's armor./A bit big.","\u2026Mister,/you're a good skeleton, right?","Dad has to stay/with His Majesty.","No letter today./\u2026I just came to see you.","I'm a squire!/Still delivering.","The armor fits now./\u2026Almost.","Dad warmed goat milk./Burned it again.","O-one\u2026!/Mom said to count!","Grandpa Skeleton!/I brought flowers!","Mom says/you're a good skeleton.","Flower delivery!","The village sent bread!/\u2026Can skeletons eat?","I'm not scared this time./Only a little.","Dad warms goat milk now./Just like you, sir.","Oh, the letter\u2026/I'll leave it here!","His Majesty's/gonna scold me\u2026","I'll leave the letter/right here!","Didn't get caught!/\u2026Is that right?","The letter\u2026/I'll put it here!","Dad's gonna/scold me\u2026","I'll come/again!","Isn't the road cold?\nThe gold is pocket money.\nThis time, it's my turn to give.","I left the forest cabin alone.\nI only mended the roof, every year.","Toby cries that he's scared.\nI was scared of you once too.\nAt twelve. Just for a moment.","I still hate goats.\nOne sniff and\nI smell that burnt milk.","The wooden sword you carved me\nis still under my bed.","People call my swordplay\n'the King's Sword.'\nIt isn't mine.","Sleep well?\nWhat you told me that night\u2014\nif I said I knew before,\nwould you believe me?","Every spring I brought flowers\nto the three of you.\nThis year my legs won't listen.\nNext year, Toby's daughter\nwill go instead.","This is my last letter.\nI was never afraid of dying.\nI was afraid of going\nwithout saying goodbye to you.","Royal Decree.\nIf it rises in the graveyard,\nopen the road. Do not fight it.","They won't obey.\nI write it anyway.","Royal Decree.\nNo one shall touch\nthe cabin in the forest.\nMend its roof every year.","He hated a leaking roof.\nEven as a skeleton.","Royal Decree.\nIts last piece of bone\nshall not be broken,\nwhatever happens.","I beg you.","Royal Decree.\nThe herald in golden armor\nshall run only\nwhile counting to three.","Count three and run,\nand he only catches you.\nHe never hurts you.\nIt was so when I was small.","Royal Decree.\nFill the pockets\nof every departing soldier\nwith plenty of gold.","My pocket money as a child,\nI spent it all on whetstones.","Royal Decree.\nThat village shall not\nbe rebuilt.","I must not build it.\nHe must.","Royal Decree.\nKeep a light burning all night\nin the castle's highest window.","So he won't lose his way.","Royal Decree.\nIf it comes in the morning\ncarrying flowers,\nall shall stand aside.\nThis time, obey.","My last request.","Royal Decree.\nStop cutting tally marks\ninto the gate pillar.","Royal Decree.\nEvery departing soldier\nshall carry one piece of bone.\nCaptains shall carry the relics.","It was the only way\nto give them back.","A different face/pulled the cart.","\ud83d\udcdc Great-grandfather's Ledger","\u300cOne whetstone \u2014 a kid.\u300d\n\u300cSays it's for Rattle's sword.\u300d","The old man doesn't know/that kid is the King.","My father said\nskeleton customers can pay later.","A soldier's coin or a skeleton's,\ngold is gold.","The decree says don't fight.\nSays nothing about trade.","Bring me anything, I'll hone it.\nEven a bone.","My father passed two years ago.\nI pull the cart now.","Great-grandpa's stone.\nStill cuts fine.","I'll give it one more pass, free.\n\u2026That kid got the same.","They say the King's grown very old.\nBetter hurry.","You'll be my last customer.\nShall I dull the edge?","Off to see someone home, you say.\nForget the blade. I'll check your joints.","Must protect\u2026/His Majesty\u2026","The skeleton\u2026 it's moving\u2026","They said grave duty was easy\u2026","Must tell\u2026 His Majesty\u2026","Don't\u2026 touch the cabin\u2026","It was\u2026 a decree\u2026","Should never\u2026 have drawn lots\u2026","No one\u2026 lives here\u2026","Flowers\u2026 in bloom\u2026","His Majesty\u2026 was waiting\u2026","For the undying King\u2026","I swore\u2026 an oath\u2026","Won't\u2026 give way\u2026","One more\u2026 mark\u2026 on the gate\u2026","The King never dies\u2026!","Carry\u2026 His Majesty\u2026","\u2026Can I go home?","Thank you.","I smell flowers.","It's not heavy anymore.","I'm going to Mom.","His Majesty\u2026 went ahead.","At home\u2026 my wife and child\u2026","The rice ball his mother packed/was still warm.","His hand shook drawing lots./He wanted to be picked.","After the army, he meant/to open a forge.","Three days' walk home./He counted every night.","Why does His Majesty send flowers/to a nameless grave?","The night before, His Majesty filled/his pocket with gold. Plenty.","The King's swordplay is strange./Not like a human's.","The kid in golden armor/always counted to three as he ran.","The undying King. A blessing, they said./His Majesty's eyes said no.","He said open the road. He refused./The first decree he ever broke.","He learned to block from His Majesty./Who taught His Majesty?","The castle's highest window./His Majesty was there every night.","This skull remembers the first/name it was called. 'Rat\u2014'","One rib/is missing.","These arms carried a baby/out of the flames.","When the child counted three and ran,/these legs chased slowly on purpose.","This skull remembers the first/name it was called. \u2026'Rattle.'","One rib is missing./\u2026It became the child's sword.","Rattle's","A relic the Church handed out as proof the Hero defeated the Demon King's Knight. Strangely, it fits perfectly.","What people called 'the Hero's bone.' It was my bone all along.","\ud83d\udc51 Leon","His breath did not stop.","\u2014 the spark Leon gave back","\u2014 the warmth left by those sent home","The skeleton fought on.","Rattle fought on.","From the castle's highest window, someone was watching.","The King did not sleep once in all that time.","Home again?","After 8 hours, it sat by the wildflowers and rested.","\u2026It sat by the wildflowers and waited.","\u300cTake it. It was always yours.\u300d \u2014 Leon","\u300cSee you tomorrow morning.\u300d \u2014 Leon","The child is waiting at the gate.","That spring too, I go to lay flowers.","A memory not yet returned \u2014 after walking to Stage {stage}.","Morning has not come yet. (after 6 a.m.)","A memory has not returned yet","How to hold a sword.","How to lift something up.","How to obey the red voice.","Only one memory can be held at a time.","More memories have returned.","How to hold a sword. How to lift.","Every memory has returned.","Still, one","goes first on the walk.","Change it any time before your first sleep. After that, each time you sleep.","When the King falls and you wake again \u2014 the next tier returns","Deep in the bones, warmth.","\ud83d\udcd6 New memory","\ud83d\udcd6 Next memory \u203a sleep again","\ud83c\udf05 It's morning \u203a sleep again","\u2709 A letter came","\ud83d\udcdc Found a royal decree","\u26a0 The strike warning changed \u2014 same spot, five times","\ud83d\udcdc The letters' signature changed","\ud83c\udfac A new scene was added to the opening","\ud83d\udcd6 \u201cThe Demon King's Ending\u201d was added to the Book of Memories","The Remembered Graveyard","Graveyard Watch Captain","Forest Patrol Captain","Village Guard Captain","Royal Guard Captain","The Nameless Graveyard","The Deep Forest","A Burned Village","The Border Castle","The procession carrying the King passed through here. Branches are broken.","Another village burned in a war long ago.","The castle the King was carried to. Its gate is shut tight.","In this forest too, some haven't made it home.","Did I burn this village too?","No banner flies over this castle either.",'Toby\'s granddaughter asked,\n"How old are you, Rattle?"\n\u2014\nInstead of answering,\nI rattled my bones.\nThe child laughed.\n','A cart by the road.\nAn old man sharpening a blade.\n\u2014\n"Royal decree says\nopen the road, don\'t fight."\n"Never said I couldn\'t trade."\n\u2014\n"A soldier\'s coin or a skeleton\'s,\ngold is gold."\n\u2014\n\u300cOld Whetstone, Roadside Smith\u300d\n','A stranger\'s face\nwas pulling the cart.\n\u2014\n"My father passed two years ago."\n"I pull the cart now."\n\u2014\n"\u2026Folks call me\nOld Whetstone too."\n','The old man opened a worn ledger.\n"Great-grandfather\'s ledger.\nOver a hundred years old."\n\u2014\n\u300cOne whetstone \u2014 a kid.\u300d\n\u300cSays it\'s for Rattle\'s sword.\u300d\n\u2014\n"The kid was a copper short.\nGreat-grandfather let it go."\n"Whoever this Rattle was."\n\u2014\nThe old man doesn\'t know\nthat kid is the King now.\n',"On the hill behind,\na grave opened.\nA skeleton rose\nand stood beside it without a word.\n\u2014\n\u300cBen \u2014 He Who Guarded the Door\u300d\n","Had it followed from the graveyard?\nAnother skeleton\npushed through the forest,\nholding something tight.\n\u2014\n\u300cElla \u2014 She Who Shielded the Child\u300d\n",'The old King fell to his knees.\n"That voice\u2026 don\'t listen\u2026"\n"Rat\u2014"\n\u2014\nFrom the King\'s chest,\na small spark\nwent into the skeleton\u2014\nno.\n\u2014\nInto me.\nIt was warm.\n\u2014\nA small hand\nwas holding my finger bone\ntight.\n\u2026Whose hand was it?\n',"A fallen cabin among the trees.\nOnly the roof was new.\n\u2014\nThe baby cried every night.\nI warmed goat milk.\nBurned it three times.\nSkeletons can't feel heat.\n\u2014\nEvery day the child went\nto the market town past the forest.\nThe words learned there,\nthe child taught to me.\n\u2014\nAt dusk\nthe door would bang open.\n\"I'm home!\"\n\u2014\nBack then I had no words,\nso I rattled my bones instead.\nThe child loved that sound\nmore than anything.\n\u2014\nEven after I learned to speak,\nI never changed that answer.\n",'The fallen King gave a small laugh.\n"\u2026Still burning the goat milk?"\n\u2014\nOnly one person in the world\nknows about the goat milk.\nThat child.\n',"Ella shook the thing\nshe had held so tight.\n[\ud6a8\uacfc\uc74c] Rattle.\n\u2014\nA wooden rattle.\nIts handle's letters were worn.\nWhy Ella had it,\nI didn't ask. I was afraid to.\n\u2014\nWhen I lifted the baby\nfrom the burning house,\nmy bones made\nthis very same sound.\n\u2014\nThe baby stopped crying\nand laughed.\n\u2014\nAt four, the child\npointed at me.\n\"Rattle!\"\n\u2014\nMade of bones taken\nfrom a thousand graves,\nit was the first name\nI ever had.\n",'"\u2026Rattle."\n"I called you that"\n"the first time, too."\n"You found your name."\n\u2014\n"You know the thing people call"\n"\'the Hero\'s bone\'?"\n"\u2026That\'s yours."\n\u2014\n"I couldn\'t keep it all."\n"Just one finger bone."\n\u2014\n[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Hero\'s Bone \u2192 Rattle\'s Bone\n','I learned words from the child.\nThe child learned\nthe sword from me.\n\u2014\n"When the big sword rises,"\n"don\'t flinch."\n"Same spot. Five times."\n"Don\'t go easy."\n"Going easy teaches nothing."\n\u2014\nWith a wooden sword,\nthe child struck my shin\nexactly five times,\nand giggled.\n\u2014\nThat night\nI asked the child\nfor one thing.\n\u2014\n"If someday"\n"I can\'t stop,"\n"you stop me."\n','The King fell, smiling.\nThe same face\nas the child with the wooden sword.\n\u2014\n"\u2026It\'s me, Rattle."\n"Leon."\n\u2014\nThe worn letters on the rattle\ncould finally be read.\n\u300cLeon\u300d\n\u2014\n"People used to say"\n"\'the Hero\'s bone\' was proof"\n"the Hero beat you."\n"\u2026That Hero was me."\n\u2014\nWhat stopped me that day\nwas these five strikes.\nThe ones I taught.\n\u2014\nLeon the Hero. Leon the King.\nThe child I raised.\nI had cut that child down\n{kingKills} times.\n','On the cabin doorframe,\nsixteen notches marking a height.\n\u2014\nThe sixteenth birthday.\nI pulled out one of my ribs\nand carved a sword.\n\u2014\n"No human blade"\n"can end me."\n"This one can."\n\u2014\nThat night, at the forest\'s edge,\nan army come for the Demon King\nlay hidden.\n\u2014\nI told the child,\n"I burned your village."\n"Go. Be with people."\n\u2014\nThe child left in tears.\nNever once looked back.\n\u2026It was good\nthat he never looked back.\n','The fallen King\nwould not let go\nof the white sword.\n\u2014\n"What you said that night."\n"I know why."\n"You wanted me to go."\n\u2014\nThe King\'s eyes stayed\na long while behind me.\n"\u2026You came as well, both of you."\n',"Ben stopped\nat the door of the burned village.\n\u2014\nLong ago, the Demon King said:\n[\ubd89\uc740] Burn.\n\u2014\nAt the door, one guard\nheld out alone.\n\"My wife and child are inside.\"\n\u2014\nI didn't know what that meant.\nSo I cut him down.\n\u2014\nA burning house.\nUnder a fallen beam,\na woman lay cold,\nwrapped around something.\n\u2014\nIn her arms, a baby\nwas shaking a rattle.\n\u2014\n\u300cBen \u2014 He Who Guarded the Door\u300d\n\u300cElla \u2014 She Who Shielded the Child\u300d\n\u2014\nIt was I who killed\nthat child's parents.\nAnd now those two\nstand beside me, guarding me.\n\u2014\nBen stepped out\none pace in front of me.\nAs he stood at the door that day.\n",'"When I was twelve, I went"\n"to the burned village"\n"past the forest."\n"On the broken nameplate"\n"were the letters on the rattle."\n\u2014\n"I knew everything."\n"And that evening too,"\n"I opened the door"\n"and said \'I\'m home.\'"\n\u2014\n"So I buried you three"\n"side by side."\n"\u2026I\'ve got three parents."\n',"The day the Demon King's\nCastle fell.\nAt the castle gate\nI met the child again,\nholding the sword from my rib.\n\u2014\n[\ubd89\uc740] Guard the castle.\nThe command lifted my arm.\nI couldn't stop.\n\u2014\nWhen the big sword rose,\nthe child did not flinch.\nSame spot. Five times.\n\u2014\nI shattered.\nBut from the child's chest\nblood was flowing too.\nMy blade had reached him first.\n\u2014\nWith breaking hands\nI pushed my spark\ninto the child.\n\"Live.\"\n\u2014\n\u2026And so that child,\nfor more than a hundred years,\ncould not die.\n",'[\ud6a8\uacfc\uc74c] Knock.\n"On the hundredth spring"\n"I knocked on your grave."\n"Knock, like that."\n\u2014\n"Every spring I walked"\n"up to your grave,"\n"and ninety-nine times,"\n"I turned back."\n\u2014\n"By the hundredth spring,"\n"the hill was hard."\n"I didn\'t think I\'d see another."\n\u2014\n"If I gave it all back, I thought"\n"I\'d go first, without a goodbye."\n"So I only gave a little."\n\u2014\n"But what rose wasn\'t you."\n"It was the command"\n"the Demon King left."\n\u2014\n[\ubd89\uc740] Bring down the king.\n[\ubd89\uc740] Take back the castle.\nIt was that voice from the start.\n\u2014\n"After that, it wouldn\'t"\n"take it from my hand."\n"The command only took by cutting."\n\u2014\n"I visited their graves too."\n"Asked them to look after you."\n"And they rose"\n"with no command at all."\n\u2014\n"Each time the spark crossed over,"\n"I knew what you remembered."\n"It\'s the same fire."\n\u2014\n"The soldiers\u2026 that\'s all on me."\n"One piece left now."\n"The command won\'t get this one."\n"When you\'re you again,"\n"I\'ll give it back."\n\u2014\n"\u2026Next time, no sword. Just come."\n"See you tomorrow morning."\n',"Soldiers lined\nboth sides of the road.\nNo one drew a sword.\n\u2014\n\u300cOpen the road.\nDo not fight.\u300d\nThe decree once broken\nwas kept at last today.\n","\u2026Ten years later.\n\u2014\nThe wildflowers on the grave\nwere still fresh.\n","\u2026Seven years later.\nFrom the two graves beside it,\nBen and Ella had risen first\nand were waiting for me.\n","\u2026Five years later.\nBy the flowers, a clumsy drawing\nof a skeleton. It was smiling.\n","\u2026Three years later.\nA wooden sword\nstood in the grave.\nOn the handle, small tooth marks.\n","\u2026Two years later.\nThe flowers, new each time I woke,\nhad wilted for the first time.\n","\u2026A year later.\nNew flowers on the wilted ones.\nBeside them, small footprints\nand drag marks of something heavy.\n","\u2026And the next morning.\nThis time, I picked the flowers.\n\u2014\nOne white wildflower from the hill.\nToday, I'm the one who brings it.\n","\u2026And again, the next morning.\nThe flower is still in my hand.\n","\u2026A few days later.\nThe flower had not changed.\nThere is still further to walk.\n","\u2026And that night.\nThe highest window\nis lit.\nMorning has not come yet.\n","There was a sound\nsomeone used to call me by.\nLike bones knocking together.\nIf I wake again, will I hear it?\n","The soldiers' strikes are strange.\nEven the angle the blade rises at\nlooks familiar.\n","Wind leaks through the ribcage.\nOne rib\nwas missing from the start.\n","Ben slows down\npassing the burned village.\nElla always stands behind me.\nLike someone who once\nshielded something.\n","The violet light\nthe King drops each time he falls.\nI knew from the very first piece.\nIt was mine all along.\n","I tried to leave behind\nwhat I was holding.\nThe hand wouldn't let go.\nIt wasn't my hand.\n","No crown. No sword.\nThe old King\nsat on the steps\nbefore the castle gate.\n",'The Demon King\'s blade stopped.\n\u2014\nThe first time it stopped\nwas in a burning house,\nwhen I lifted a baby.\nThe second time is now.\n\u2014\n"\u2026You stopped."\n"This time, you did."\n\u2014\n"So I raised my sword every time."\n"So you\'d never forget the five."\n\u2014\n"{kingVisits} times."\n"That\'s how often you came."\n"I counted every one."\n\u2014\nThe King reached out\nand laid a hand on my skull.\n"The last piece"\n"I can only give back like this."\n\u2014\nSixteen years came back at once.\nGoat milk. A wooden sword.\nSixteen notches.\n\u2014\nThe last faces\nof those I cut down. Every one.\nAll of them were guarding\nsomething from me.\n\u2014\nThose faces\nhad still not made it home.\n\u2014\nThe King grew light.\nI caught that child in my arms.\n\u2014\nElla came close\nand put the rattle in his hand.\nBen laid a hand on my shoulder.\n\u2014\n"\u2026You stayed with him to the end."\n"Both of you."\n\u2014\n"Hey, Rattle."\n"I never once called you this."\n\u2014\n"\u2026Dad."\n\u2014\n"I\'m home."\n\u2014\nThe answer I had never\nonce said aloud,\nI said for the first time.\n"\u2026Welcome home."\n\u2014\n[\ud6a8\uacfc\uc74c] Rattle.\nThe rattle fell to the floor.\n\u2014\nSkeletons cannot cry.\nSo that day, at the castle gate,\nfor a long time,\nthere was only the sound of bones.\n',"The wildflower I brought,\nI laid on that child's chest.\nOver the castle,\nno banner was raised.\n\u2014\nOn the gate pillar,\na white bone sword\nand one royal decree.\n\u300cStop counting the marks now.\u300d\n{tally}\n\u2014\nThat spring,\nthe Forgotten Graveyard.\nBetween Ben and Ella,\nwhere I lay for a hundred years,\nthat child was laid to rest.\n\u2014\nOn the grave that had no name,\nI carved a name.\n\u300cLeon \u2014 the Child Who Came Home\u300d\nThis time, all three have names.\n\u2014\nIn the burned village,\nthe first house went up.\nI built it.\nThe roof doesn't leak.\n\u2014\nNext door,\nToby keeps goats.\n\u2014\nNow I lay the flowers.\nEvery spring.\nAs many times as it takes.\n",'[\ubd89\uc740] Take it back.\n\u2014\nThe blade fell.\nSame spot. Five times.\n\u2014\n"\u2026It\'s okay."\n"As many times as it takes."\n\u2014\nSoldiers took the King\non their backs and ran.\nHis breath had not stopped yet.\n\u2014\nThe last piece\ndid not come by the sword.\n\u2014\n\u2026And the next morning,\nthe King was again\nsitting before the castle gate.\n',"The Demon King's command shattered.\nIts pieces lodged\nin the bones of those I'd cut down\nand raised them again.\n\u2014\nThose I struck down,\n{endKillCount} of them.\nStill standing in the road,\nunable to go home.\n\u2014\nI walk again.\nTo break the pieces, one by one,\nand send them home.\n","All {endKillCount}.\nEvery last one,\nsent home.\n\u2014\nStill, I walk.\nThose I cut down\nmore than a hundred years ago\nare still on the road.\n","A memory held on the walk.\nFive times, just as I taught.\n","A memory held on the walk.\nEmpty arms remembered how to hold.\n","A memory held on the walk.\nThe arm the command raised,\nI lowered.\n","[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Swordsman Tier 1 \u2014 Counter\nEven when the big sword rises,\nno flinching.\nBlock, and strike back.\n","[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Guardian Tier 1 \u2014 Take It on the Back\nArms that once carried something.\nLet the back take the blow.\nFalling comes after.\n","[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Berserker Tier 1 \u2014 Rage\n[\ubd89\uc740] Rage.\nThe bones burned hot first.\n","[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Swordsman Tier 2 \u2014 Five Times\nA rusted sword stuck by a grave.\nIt was someone's, long ago.\n\u2014\nOn the fifth strike,\nit always hits the same spot.\nWhose habit is that?\n","[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Guardian Tier 2 \u2014 A Hand to Hold You Up\nA door from the burned village\nbecame a shield.\n\u2014\nEach time I started to fall,\nElla shook the rattle.\n\u2014\n[\ud6a8\uacfc\uc74c] Rattle.\nAs if to say, get up.\n","[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Berserker Tier 2 \u2014 Don't Think\n[\ubd89\uc740] Don't think.\n[\ubd89\uc740] Just cut.\nThe voice grew a little louder.\n",'[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Swordsman Tier 3 \u2014 The Wooden Sword\nOld Whetstone\nheld out great-grandpa\'s stone.\nThe rust came off easily.\n\u2014\nThe wooden sword in the grave,\nI slung on my back.\n\u2014\n"Don\'t go easy."\n"Going easy teaches nothing."\nThis time, it\'s my turn to learn.\n',"[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Guardian Tier 3 \u2014 He Who Guarded the Door\nLifted the bar of the castle gate.\n\u2014\nA bone Ben threw\nknocked a strike aside.\n\u2014\nNo one told him to.\nAs if he had stood at a door.\n",'[\uc2dc\uc2a4\ud15c] Berserker Tier 3 \u2014 Cut\n[\ubd89\uc740] Cut.\n"Remember this sword?"\nBefore I could answer,\nthe arm moved.\n',"{name} \xb7 {title}","Rattle waited for {away}."],t.li)
